8257520,2024-02-01,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"Wednesday XX/XX/ Dear CFPB employees, Subject : Complaint - Request for Proof of Late Payment under 15 USC 1666b To Whom It May Concern : I am writing to file a formal complaint against XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX and XXXX XXXX regarding a disputed late payment on my consumer report. I have requested proof from XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Director of Compliance and XXXX XXXX CEO, that the payments were indeed late based on the specifications of 15 USC 1666b, but they have failed to provide the required information. 

I am a diligent consumer who is well aware of my rights under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and other applicable consumer financial protection laws. I recently corresponded with XXXX  XXXX, specifically with XXXX XXXX and XXXX XXXX, regarding the late payments that they have listed on my consumer report. I requested in good faith the necessary documents to prove that the information required by section 1666b of 15 USC was mailed out or delivered 21 days before the payment due date. 

However, they have not provided any evidence or documentation to support their claim of a late payment. I assert that according to the law, a creditor can not treat a payment as late without complying with the stipulations outlined in 15 USC 1666b. I have not received proof of such compliance. 

This refusal by XXXX XXXX and XXXX XXXX to provide the requested information is a clear violation of section 15 USC 1681a ( 2 ) ( A ) ( i ) of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and section 15 USC 1666b & 1637 ( b ) of the applicable title. 

I hereby demand that XXXX  XXXX, XXXX XXXX and XXXX XXXX provide the required information and proof of the alleged late payment within 10 calendar days from the receipt of this complaint. Any correspondence NOT including the proof I am demanding will be deemed a failure to comply. Failure to comply with this request will be deemed as an admission that the reported late payment is erroneous, and I insist on its immediate deletion from my consumer report. 

Furthermore, I will be submitting this complaint and the related facts and correspondence to the XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX and you guys, the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) for further investigation and appropriate action if XXXX  XXXX, XXXX XXXX and XXXX XXXX do not rectify this matter promptly. 

Thank you for your attention to this serious issue. I look forward to a swift resolution and the accurate representation of my consumer report. 

Sincerely, XXXX.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NV,89102,,Web,2024-02-01,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
