I maintain that Wise should be sanctioned for their draconian overreaction to my mistaken yet good-faith attempt to transfer my XXXX  on XX/XX/XXXX. I would also ask that they reinstate my accounts to enable me to continue to make use of their services. Further, Wise has arrogated some XXXX XXXX of my money and failed to honor my complaint within the promised XXXX calendar days. 

The rash reactions of Wise have caused me considerable stress for more than XXXX months. It is exasperating and upsetting suddenly not to have access to a convenient, familiar, and reasonably priced way to convert and transfer my pension payments and company earnings from XXXX to XXXX. As mentioned, together they represent more than XXXX XXXX  of my monthly income. I was forced to borrow some money from my home equity line of credit to pay some bills on time, owing to the lack of service and even any communication on the part of Wise. I also had to re-learn how to arrange expensive wire transfers from my XXXX  personal and business accounts to my XXXX  accounts. 

In summary : The relationship between Wise.com and myself, as a consumer, is asymmetrical. Wise is a corporation that deals with currency conversions and transfers professionally and on a full-time basis. I use their services only occasionally and incidentally. Wise should therefore be fully prepared to deal with an anomaly like my XX/XX/XXXX transfer. They might be expected, as professionals, to directly return the money I mistakenly sent from a personal account to that same account and remind me via email that all transfers to my business account in XXXX  must come from the business account in XXXX that they have on file for me. Instead, they de-activated my account without comment. When I asked the customer service department why Wise de-activated the account ( as I was still unaware of my mistake ), they brusquely referred me, without further comment, to section XXXX in the contract. I checked the contract, and there is no section XXXX, just a very long section XXXX ( although there are many other sections with subsections, like XXXX, for example ). I had to check my bank accounts to discover my error. The individuals working in their customer service department informed me that they themselves have no insight into operations. If Wise had nipped the problem in the bud, that is, if they had acted professionally, I would have apologized and resubmitted my requested transfer, and my dealings with Wise would have continued unblemished. As it turned out, they proceeded to aggravate the situation, creating a cascade effect with their de-activation then re-activation then de-activation of my account, setting up the series of misunderstandings about refunds and re-submitted funds that led to their definitive termination of my accounts, despite hundreds and hundreds of untarnished transactions carried out to our mutual satisfaction and benefit throughout most of the companys existence. I thus maintain that the blame for this outcome is also asymmetrical. 

It is my hope that the Consumer Financial Protection Board will agree with me and cite Wise.com for erratic and unprofessional treatment of a client and confiscating funds from that client ; the remedies would be for Wise to reinstate my accounts and to refund my money, with an apology and another offer of some free transfers.

