8333278,2024-02-12,"Payday loan, title loan, personal loan, or advance loan",Installment loan,Getting the loan,,"Dear Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, I am writing to express my concern over misleading communication practices employed by Upstart in their loan approval process in partnership with XXXX Specifically, this pertains to a {$1500.00} relief loan application I submitted in the week of XX/XX/2024. 

Upon my initial application, I received a pre-approval notification for the loan. After a week, during which there were no changes in my financial status, I submitted the application for final approval. To my surprise, the final approval email stated that I was "" APPROVED '', but it also mentioned that this approval was contingent on certain undisclosed disqualifiers. 

This language is problematic and misleading. An approval that is contingent on further conditions should not be termed as a definitive "" approval '', but rather as a continuation of the pre-approval stage. This miscommunication gives a false impression to the consumer. 

Moreover, the stated disqualifier for my application an increase in debt since my initial application is factually incorrect. I had not incurred any additional debt during that period. 

The purpose of this complaint is to urge the CFPB to enforce more transparent and accurate language in loan approval communications. It is crucial that terms like "" APPROVED '' are used appropriately and accurately to prevent misleading consumers. The current practice of indicating final approval, while still being in a conditional pre-approval stage, is deceptive and needs to be addressed. 

