8436028,2024-02-28,"Payday loan, title loan, personal loan, or advance loan",Installment loan,Problem with the payoff process at the end of the loan,,"I applied for a home improvement loan through MOSAIC ( aka XXXXsolar mosaic ) that was approved on XX/XX/XXXX for {$11000.00}. There was a 12 month interest free promotion, which ended on XX/XX/XXXX, at which point 8.24 % interest would be charged for the 12 month period if the principal was not paid in full. I paid the full balance owed using an online web portal on XX/XX/XXXX and received an email from Mosaic on XX/XX/XXXX saying the payment had been received. On XX/XX/XXXX I received an email from Mosaic that my payment had failed due to "" insufficient funds ''. 

I saw the email on XX/XX/XXXX and called Mosaic to see why it had failed, since I still had sufficient funds in the account. I initially spoke to a supervisor who was extremely rude, but then asked to speak to an escalation manage and spoke with XXXX XXXX about the situation. As he looked through the payment details, we realized that Mosaic had attempted to pull the funds from my checking account, when I had indicated in the web form via a radial button that the target account was a savings account. I use a credit union where both my checking accounts and saving accounts have the same account number. Because they attempted to pull the funds from my checking account instead of my savings account, that's why the payment failed. I offered to pay the principal balance if Mosaic would waive the accrued interest fees and he said he could not do that. XXXX said he would esclate the issue to his executive in charge of disputes and call me back later that day or the following monday. I offered to pay the principal balance that day, but he said it would be better to wait until we received a resopnse on the dispute. I never received a call back, email, or letter in response. 

On XX/XX/XXXX I called in again and spoke to XXXX. He said XXXX had left the company and he could not see record in my file of a formal dispute escalation request. He said he would submit the formal request and I would receive a response back. 
I paid the principal due at that time and have that confirmation number. I never received a call, email, or letter back.

